abstract:
The antithesis is human. Harken, dear;
There’s too much abstract willing, purposing,
In this poor world. We talk by aggregates,

abstinence:
Far ends of tired days;
It half endears the abstinence,
And pain is missed in praise.

absolution:
Some day, when there's another in my stead;
Again you'll feel the need of absolution,
And you will go to her, and bow your head,
